yes(641,'B','The enthalpy change is H(products) − H(reactants). A negative value of −65.7 kJ mol⁻¹ means that the products have lower enthalpy and heat is released. It does not determine the reaction speed.',[RX],question='RS(aq) + HF(aq) → RF(s) + HS(aq), ΔH = −65.7 kJ mol⁻¹. What can be deduced?',options=['The reactants have lower enthalpy than the products','The reactants have higher enthalpy than the products','The reaction is slow','A large amount of heat is absorbed'],audit='Restored arrow/Δ and repaired duplicated reactant/product wording in optionA.',check='enthalpy-sign')
